  {
    // The Dzhanibekov effect (the tennis racket theorem): a body spins steadily about the
    // axis of its largest moment of inertia or its smallest, not about the middle one. The
    // satellite's long axis is its middle one. Spun about it at 36°/s with a 1°/s wobble, it
    // turns itself end over end after about 15 s, then back every 30 s, for as long as it
    // is left alone. RCS (R) with SAS (T) stops it.
    id: "dzhanibekov",
    name: "Tumbling satellite",
    description: "A satellite spun about its middle axis of inertia, which it cannot keep spinning about: it flips end over end every 30 s (the Dzhanibekov effect). R and T stop it.",
